    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Associate-Professor_R-2589-1": {
      "title": "Associate Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University's School of Nursing invites applications for a tenure track position at the rank of Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing to begin Spring 2027. This position will teach at the undergraduate and/or graduate level as needed. Teaching efforts must demonstrate activities that encourage interaction with other students, faculty, the university, and/or the community, and support student success and learning in the classroom and clinical setting. The successful candidate must have a record of continuous professional development and engage in scholarly activities such as research, publishing, and presenting. Service to the University through committee work and participation in special projects and activities, service to students through academic and career guidance and participation in and support of student activities, and service to the community through activities utilizing professional knowledge and expertise, are expected of this position. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS A doctorate degree in Nursing conferred by the date of hire An unencumbered RN license in the state of Louisiana Two years clinical experience as an RN Must be committed to working with diversity PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Prior teaching experience APRN Certification DESIRED KNOWLEDGE, ABILITIES AND SKILLS Proficient computer skills (i.e., word processing, presentation software, spreadsheets, etc.) Effective interpersonal communication skills REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter Resume/Vita Copies of Transcripts (Only an unofficial transcript for the Highest degree is required at application. Official transcripts for all degrees will be required upon employment.) Posting Close Date October 26, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Professor-Dean-of-Nursing_R-2590": {
      "title": "Professor/Dean of Nursing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University invites applications for the position of Dean of the College of Nursing. The University seeks an innovative, collaborative, student-centered, and externally engaged academic leader who will advance excellence in nursing education, expand Southeastern’s contribution to Louisiana’s healthcare workforce, and help shape the future of the College. The Dean serves as the chief academic and administrative officer of the College and reports to the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs. As a member of the University’s academic leadership team, the Dean provides strategic leadership for academic programs, faculty and staff, enrollment and student success, accreditation, resource stewardship, external partnerships, advancement, and innovation. The appointment comes at an important moment for Southeastern. The College of Nursing is entering a new era as a focused, standalone academic college, providing the next Dean with the opportunity to build upon strong academic programs, exceptional student outcomes, significant enrollment, and extensive healthcare partnerships while establishing a clear vision for future growth and distinction. Southeastern Louisiana University is a progressive regional, comprehensive university that enrolls approximately 15,700 graduate and undergraduate students. The University’s home, Hammond, is at the crossroads of Interstates 55 and 12 in the heart of Louisiana’s thriving Northshore, the fastest growing region in the state. It is centrally located within an hour’s drive of New Orleans, Baton Rouge (the state capitol), and the Mississippi Gulf Coast, and affords extensive cultural, recreational, and research opportunities. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS An earned Doctorate in Nursing or a closely related field from an accredited institution. A current, unencumbered Registered Nursing license and eligibility for licensure in Louisiana. A record of teaching, scholarship, professional practice, and/or service appropriate for appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. Significant progressively responsible academic administrative or leadership experience. Demonstrated knowledge of nursing accreditation, regulatory standards, program assessment, and professional licensure requirements. Experience with academic budgeting, personnel management, and resource allocation. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with faculty, staff, students, institutional leaders, and external partners. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Particular consideration will be given to candidates with demonstrated success in several of the following areas: Leadership of a college, school, department, or major academic nursing program. Strategic planning and organizational change. Undergraduate and graduate nursing education. Enrollment growth and strategic program development. Student recruitment, retention, progression, graduation, and licensure success. Clinical and healthcare-system partnerships. Faculty recruitment, retention, mentorship, and development. CCNE accreditation and state regulatory processes. Graduate and doctoral program development. Online, hybrid, accelerated, or alternative educational pathways. Simulation, digital health, healthcare technology, or artificial intelligence. Grants, contracts, philanthropy, or other external resource development. Workforce development and community engagement. DESIRED KNOWLEDGE, ABILITIES, AND SKILLS Knowledge of relevant accreditation, curriculum, and program development processes applicable to the various disciplines within the college Ability to work collaboratively and effectively with department heads, faculty, staff, and other deans and administrators at all levels within the college and University Committed to recruiting diverse and inclusive faculty, staff, and students REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter addressing qualifications Curriculum Vitae Names and contact information for 3-5 professional references Transcripts for terminal degree (all official transcripts are required upon employment) Application Deadline: For full consideration, submit materials by November 3, 2026. Review will continue until the position is filled. All applications must be submitted through Southeastern’s Workday system. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. Search and selection subject to approval by the Board of Supervisors of the University of Louisiana System. ~Southeastern is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer~ Posting Close Date October 26, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Instructor-of-Mathematics_R-2580": {
      "title": "Instructor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University's Department of Mathematics invites applications for an Instructor position. Duties include teaching at the undergraduate level and participating in service activities at the department, college, and university levels. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s Degree in Mathematics or a related field from an accredited university by hire date PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Proven record of excellence in teaching Previous high school and/or post-secondary teaching Must be committed to working with diversity REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter Resume/Vita Copies of Transcripts (Only an unofficial transcript for the Highest degree is required at application. Official transcripts for all degrees will be required upon employment.) Posting Close Date October 15, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
