    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Department-Head-of-Chemistry-and-Physics_R-2594": {
      "title": "Department Head of Chemistry and Physics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University's College of Science and Technology in Hammond, LA invites applications for a collaborative, forward-thinking Department Head to lead its Department of Chemistry and Physics, beginning Spring or Summer 2027. This twelve-month administrative position is primarily responsible for advancing the culture of academic excellence, where distinction in teaching, research, scholarship, and service is expected and rewarded. As the link between the faculty and the central administration, the head is expected to provide leadership for curriculum development, implementation, and the assessment of student learning. The head is also responsible for managing all budgets related to the department and teaching undergraduate courses within it. The head should be a driving force behind the development and enhancement of curricula, research programs, scholarly efforts, and strategic initiatives that further the department's and college's strategic plans, including recruiting and retaining a diverse student population, and developing partnerships with industry and the local community. Southeastern Louisiana University is located in Hammond, less than 50 miles from New Orleans and Baton Rouge, with an enrollment of more than 15,000 students. The Department of Chemistry and Physics offers a Chemistry B.S. with concentrations in Chemistry (ACS certified), Biochemistry, and Interdisciplinary Studies, and a Physics B.S. with concentrations in Physics, Engineering Physics, and Applied Physics, including dual-degree partnerships with two LSU campuses, and serves approximately 85 chemistry and 40 physics undergraduate students. Details about the department can be found at https://www.southeastern.edu/department-of-chemistry-and-physics/. Key Responsibilities: 1. Oversees strategic (short- and long-range) planning, direction, and development of the department. 2. Coordinates and administers rules and academic standards regarding undergraduate and graduate instruction, curricula, and scheduling. 3. Plans, initiates, and oversees the execution of organizational, operational, and academic programs for the department. 4. Leads faculty development and recruitment; evaluates faculty in accordance with tenure and promotion guidelines; makes recommendations for faculty appointments, promotions, and compensation; and provides support for fundraising, proposal writing, and developing new programs in congruence with the University's mission. 5. Manages and allocates the department's budget to support academic, research, and operational needs, including developing budget requests for the Dean. 6. Coordinates departmental policies and procedures. 7. Represents the department at formal functions and in public relations efforts, including speaking engagements and community outreach. 8. Works with and chairs University committees as assigned; assists the Dean in formulating College policies and procedures. 9. Maintains operational procedures, rules, and standards relating to faculty and staff. 10. Oversees course scheduling and recommends implementation or removal of courses, concentrations, and programs. 11. Advises the Dean and Provost on academic matters concerning the department. 12. Leads assessment of student learning outcomes and program effectiveness. 13. Champions the growth of research initiatives, including interdisciplinary collaboration and external funding opportunities. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Terminal degree (doctorate) in a discipline directly related to Chemistry or Physics from an accredited university by hire date. Credentials commensurate with a faculty appointment at the associate or full professor level. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Demonstrated success in academic administration, including leading teams and managing budgets and programs, or relevant industry experience that connects classroom instruction with real-world practice. Proven experience cultivating beneficial relationships and partnerships with regional industry. A strong record of excellence in research and teaching, reflecting a commitment to high academic standards and innovative practices. Demonstrated ability to lead and support faculty, staff, and students from a variety of backgrounds and lived experiences. Experience with accreditation processes and relevant professional societies, including program assessment, continuous improvement, and compliance with ACS accreditation standards. Exceptional interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with diverse stakeholders and foster an inclusive environment. Candidates who progress beyond the initial stage will be asked for the names and contact information for three professional references, including email addresses, telephone numbers, their current employers and their positions. At least two references should be able to provide commentary specifically addressing the applicant's interpersonal and communication skills. References will not be contacted until after the initial screening and upon first informing the applicant. REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter describing specific interest in the position Current Resume/Vita Leadership Statement detailing how the candidate's experiences make them prepared for and interested in this position Copies of Transcripts (only an unofficial transcript for the highest degree is required at application; official transcripts for all degrees will be required upon employment) Questions concerning this position, please contact: Dr. Gerard Blanchard Chair, Department Head Screening Committee Department of Chemistry and Physics Southeastern Louisiana University SLU 10878, Hammond, LA 70402 Gerard.Blanchard@Southeastern.edu Application Details: The desired starting date is either January 1, 2027, or June 1, 2027. Salary is commensurate with experience and qualifications. Applications will be reviewed upon receipt and receive full consideration until November 9, 2026. The review process will continue until the position is filled. Posting Close Date November 9, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Department-Head-of-Industrial-and-Engineering-Technology_R-2595": {
      "title": "Department Head of Industrial and Engineering Technology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University's College of Science and Technology invites applications for the position of Department Head for The Department of Industrial and Engineering Technology (IET). The Department is seeking an innovative, dedicated leader to serve as Department Head. This position requires a collaborative and strategic leader to guide the department in achieving academic and administrative excellence. As the chief academic and administrative officer of the IET department, the Department Head will foster a culture that prioritizes and celebrates teaching, research, service, and industry collaborations. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to advancing the department's mission and have a proven track record of academic leadership, budget management, and fostering research and academic excellence. The Department Head is active in teaching undergraduate and graduate courses and maintains a research program appropriate for a department in a college with undergraduate and master's degree programs. The position is a full-time, 12-month appointment. Key Responsibilities: 1. Provide visionary leadership and serve as the primary liaison connecting faculty with university administration, as well as faculty with students. 2. Oversee curriculum development and implementation across three academic programs: Industrial Technology (IT), Engineering Technology (ET), and Occupational, Safety, Health and Environment (OSH&E), ensuring alignment with industry trends and academic standards. 3. Lead efforts to assess student learning outcomes and program effectiveness. 4. Manage and allocate the department’s budget to effectively support academic, research, and operational needs. 5. Champion and expand high-impact research research initiatives by driving interdisciplinary collaboration and helping faculty to secure external funding. 6. Foster an inclusive environment that supports faculty development and rewards excellence in teaching, research, and service. 7. Drive initiatives that align with department, college, and university strategic goals, advancing the reputation and impact of the department's degree programs. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Doctoral degree in a discipline closely related to Engineering, Industrial Technology, or OSH&E by hire date. A proven record of excellence in research, teaching, and leadership, with qualifications that support appointment at the rank of Associate or Full Professor. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Demonstrated success in academic administration, with experience in leading teams and managing budgets and programs, or relevant industry experience that can be leveraged to enrich the classroom instruction and connect theory with real-world practice. Proven track record of building and sustaining strategic partnerships with regional industry partners to advance departmental growth, align programs with evolving workforce technologies, and expand student career opportunities. A strong record of excellence in research and teaching that reflects commitment to high academic standards and innovative practices. Exceptional interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with diverse stakeholders and foster an inclusive environment. Demonstrated commitment to equal opportunity and providing a supportive environment for everyone in an academic or industry setting. Experience with the procedures for maintaining ABET and/or ATMAE accreditation, including program assessment for student advising and student outcomes, continuous improvement processes, and compliance with accreditation standards. Candidates who progress beyond the initial stage will be asked for the names and contact information for five professional references, including email addresses, telephone numbers, their current employers and their positions. At least two references should be able to provide commentary specifically addressing the applicant's interpersonal and communication skills. References will not be contacted until after the initial screening and upon first informing the applicant. REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter explaining interest in the Department Head position Resume/Vita Copies of Transcripts (Only an unofficial transcript for the highest degree is required at application. Official transcripts for all degrees will be required upon employment.) Teaching philosophy For further inquiries, please contact Dr. Ephraim Massawe, Chair of the Department Head Search Committee, at ephraim.massawe@southeastern.edu or by phone at (+1) 985-549-2243 or by mail at the Department of Industrial and Engineering Technology, SLU 10847, Hammond, LA 70402. For full consideration, please apply by November 9th, 2026. The position will remain open until it is filled. Posting Close Date November 9, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Assistant-Professor-of-Management_R-2584": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University’s Department of Management and Business Administration is accepting applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Management at the rank of Assistant/Associate Professor. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate/graduate Management courses, engage in scholarly research/professional activities sufficient to establish and maintain AACSB qualifications, and provide service to the department, college, and university. Required Qualifications: Candidates for appointment at the Assistant/Associate Professor level must have completed an earned doctorate in Management or a related field by the start date. Preferred Qualifications: Candidates should have a strong desire for teaching, established scholarly productivity or potential for establishing and maintaining scholarly activities and service. While candidates in all areas of Management will be considered, preference will be given to applicants with experience, coursework, credentials, etc. in the area of Strategy. Required Documents: Cover Letter Resume/Vita Copies of Transcripts (Only an unofficial transcript for the highest degree is required at application. Official transcripts for all degrees will be required upon employment.) Posting Close Date November 2, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Department-Head-of-English-and-World-Languages_R-2601": {
      "title": "Department Head of English and World Languages",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University’s College of Arts, Humanities, and Social Sciences invites applications for an inspiring, collaborative leader to serve as the Department Head for the Department of English and World Languages. The department offers undergraduate programs in English and World Languages, including study in creative writing, literary studies, English education, French, Spanish, and dual languages, as well as an undergraduate TESOL certificate. The department also offers the Master of Arts in English with areas of study including creative writing, literary studies, literacy and language, professional writing, and publishing studies. The Department Head is the chief academic and administrative officer of the department, serving a 12-month appointment and reporting to the Dean. The position carries both administrative and faculty responsibilities, including teaching, scholarship/creative activity, and service appropriate to the scope of the department. The successful candidate will provide strategic, transparent, and collaborative leadership for a multidisciplinary department and will work with faculty and staff to advance academic quality, student success, enrollment, and the visibility and impact of the department. Key Responsibilities: 1. Provide collaborative leadership in curriculum development, program review, assessment, strategic planning, and academic innovation across English and World Languages. 2. Mentor, support, and evaluate faculty and staff; recruit new faculty; and promote professional development, scholarly/creative activity, and a collegial departmental culture. 3. Manage departmental budgets and resources responsibly, establish priorities, and advocate effectively for the department. 4. Oversee course scheduling, enrollment management, academic advising processes, and the effective delivery of undergraduate and graduate programs. 5. Develop and implement strategies that support student recruitment, persistence, retention, graduation, and career readiness. 6. Support the continued strength and development of the department’s graduate programs, language programs, writing-focused curricula, dual enrollment, and other distinctive academic initiatives. 7. Foster collaboration across the disciplines represented in the department and build partnerships with other academic units, schools, community organizations, and external stakeholders. 8. Support appropriate use of emerging technologies and evolving pedagogical practices in teaching, learning, and scholarship. 9. Advance the visibility of the department and support outreach, grant development, fundraising, and partnership-building activities as appropriate. 10. Represent the department within the College and University and with community and professional constituencies, while promoting shared governance and transparent decision-making. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Terminal degree from an accredited university in a discipline represented within English, World Languages, or a closely related field by hire date. Record of teaching, scholarship and/or creative activity, and service warranting appointment as a tenured associate or full professor in an appropriate departmental discipline. Minimum of six years of successful full-time college or university teaching at the assistant professor level or above. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience effectively leading an academic department or other complex academic unit. Experience leading or supporting graduate education and/or multidisciplinary programs in English, languages, writing, linguistics, or related fields. Demonstrated success with student recruitment, enrollment growth, retention, or program revitalization. Experience mentoring faculty across career stages and supporting faculty research, scholarship, or creative activity. Evidence of successful interdisciplinary, community, K-12, or external partnerships. Experience with grant development, fundraising, or securing external resources. Experience guiding organizational change, curriculum restructuring, or the development of new academic programs or credentials. A record of leadership that supports both the humanities’ intellectual mission and students’ preparation for careers and graduate study. Evidence of excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching and a commitment to student success. Experience with curriculum development, program review, and assessment. Experience with personnel, budget, scheduling, or other significant academic administrative responsibilities. DESIRED KNOWLEDGE, ABILITIES, AND SKILLS Strong interpersonal, organizational, written, and oral communication skills. Demonstrated ability to lead collaboratively, build consensus, and work effectively across multiple disciplines and areas of specialization. Demonstrated academic leadership experience, such as service as a department head/chair, associate or assistant chair, program director/coordinator, or comparable role. Demonstrated commitment to shared governance, transparency, integrity, and inclusive academic leadership. Candidates who progress beyond the initial stage will be asked for the names and contact information for three professional references, including email addresses, telephone numbers, their current employers and their positions. At least two references should be able to provide commentary specifically addressing the applicant's interpersonal and communication skills. References will not be contacted until after the initial screening and upon first informing the applicant. REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter addressing qualifications. Resume/Curriculum Vitae Copies of Transcripts (Only an unofficial transcript for the Highest degree is required at application. Official transcripts for all degrees will be required upon employment.) Questions concerning this position should be directed to the search committee Chair, Dr. Ziba Rashidian, ziba.rashidian@selu.edu. The desired start date is July 1, 2027. Application Deadline: For full consideration, submit materials by November 30, 2026. The search will continue until the position is filled. All applications must be submitted through Southeastern’s Workday system. Posting Close Date November 30, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Administrative-Assistant-3_R-2609-1": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant 3",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nSoutheastern Louisiana University’s Dean of Students invites applications for the position of Administrative Assistant 3. The Administrative Assistant 3 provides primary administrative support to the Director of Administrative Operations and office staff while coordinating a wide range of administrative, operational, purchasing, timekeeping, and customer service functions. The position supports office scheduling and logistics, maintains administrative and purchasing records, assists with budget monitoring, processes authorized purchasing activities, coordinates equipment and inventory needs, and serves as the primary timekeeping coordinator for the Graduate Assistant and Student Workers. The position also supervises student workers and supports their training and professional development. The successful candidate will be organized, detail-oriented, service-focused, and able to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced, student-centered environment. The position requires effective communication, strong administrative skills, attention to accuracy, and the ability to work collaboratively with the Director, Graduate Assistant, student workers, and campus partners. Hourly Rate: $13.77 AN IDEAL CANDIDATE SHOULD POSSESS THE FOLLOWING COMPETENCIES Communicating Effectively : The ability to relay information correctly and appropriately to connect people and ideas Demonstrating Accountability : The ability to accept ownership for your actions, behaviors, performance, and decisions Focusing on Customers:  The ability to serve the needs of those who support and/or rely on the services provided EXAMS AND LICENSE REQUIRMENTS No Civil Service test score is required in order to be considered for this vacancy Applicants must possess a valid driver’s license and be able to be certified through the Southeastern Defensive Driving Course MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS Two years of experience in administrative services. SUBSTITUTIONS Every 15 semester hours earned from an accredited college or university will be credited as six months of experience. Failure to provide your qualifying work experience will result in your application not being considered Any qualifying experience that is based on college credit/hours will require a transcript for verification Any college hours or degree must be from a school accredited by one of the following regional accrediting bodies:  the Middle States Commission on Higher Education; the New England Association of Schools and Colleges; the Higher Learning Commission; the Northwest Commission on Colleges and Universities; the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools; and the Western Association of Schools and Colleges. When applying, you should list all Education and Work Experience on this application. When listing your Work Experience, indicate if the job was full-time or part-time and what percentage of time you spent on each of the duties listed. This information will be used to determine if you meet the Minimum Qualifications of the position. If complete information is not listed, it may result in your application not being considered. *Resumes WILL NOT be accepted in lieu of completed education and experience sections on your application. There is no guarantee that everyone who applies to this posting will be interviewed. The hiring supervisor/manager has 90 days from the closing date of the posting to make a hiring decision. Click Here to View the Civil Service Job Spec   Posting Close Date October 27, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. HR Contact If you have questions about this position, the application process or need special accommodations, please call the Human Resources Office at (985) 549-2001 or send an email to jobs@southeastern.edu."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/HVAC-Refrigeration-Master-Mech_R-2625": {
      "title": "HVAC Refrigeration Master Mech",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nSoutheastern Louisiana University's Department of Physical Plant Services invites applications for the position of HVAC Refrigeration Master Mechanic. This position is responsible for a variety of tasks relating to installation, repairs, and maintenance of HVAC systems and refrigeration units across the campus. As the HVAC Refrigeration Master Mechanic, the ability to exercise independent judgment will be necessary, as this position will serve as a lead worker over multiple HVAC Refrigeration Mechanic positions. Work Schedule: Mon - Thurs 6:30 am - 4:15 pm with 45 min. lunch; Fri 6:30 am - 11:30 am Hourly Rate: $22.52 EXAM, LICENSE, AND SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS Applicants must possess a valid driver’s license and be able to be certified through the Southeastern Defensive Driving Course Appropriate EPA refrigerant recycling and recovery certification for technicians (as required under Section 608 of the Clean Air Act, 1990). Southeastern requires a Type IV, Universal Certification. Please note that Southeastern will allow the candidate selected for the job up to 30 days to acquire the required certification. Additional information regarding technician certification requirements and programs may be obtained by calling the Stratospheric Ozone Protection Hotline at (800) 296-1996 (10am-4pm Eastern Time, Monday-Friday except federal holidays) or by visiting the EPA's Stratospheric Ozone Depletion Web Site at www.epa.gov/ozone/title6/608. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Three years of experience or training in the installation and/or maintenance of heating, ventilating, or air conditioning systems. Failure to provide your qualifying work experience will result in your application not being considered When applying, you should list all Education and Work Experience on this application. When listing your Work Experience, indicate if the job was full-time or part-time and what percentage of time you spent on each of the duties listed. This information will be used to determine if you meet the Minimum Qualifications of the position. If complete information is not listed, it may result in your application not being considered. *Resumes WILL NOT be accepted in lieu of completed education and experience sections on your application. There is no guarantee that everyone who applies to this posting will be interviewed. The hiring supervisor/manager has 90 days from the closing date of the posting to make a hiring decision. Click Here to View the Civil Service Job Spec Posting Close Date October 20, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. HR Contact If you have questions about this position, the application process or need special accommodations, please call the Human Resources Office at (985) 549-2001 or send an email to jobs@southeastern.edu."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Associate-Professor-of-Communication-and-Media-Studies_R-2612": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Communication and Media Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University's Department of Communication and Media Studies invites applications for one tenured Associate Professor position. The successful candidate will have significant experience in Digital Media - Sports/Entertainment, understanding the mechanics of how the industry works and will be able to develop and train students in strategic communication and sports and entertainment production. We are an applied program with a focus on preparing students for meaningful work as communication strategists and content creators for industry. The successful candidates will be expected to demonstrate excellence in online, asynchronous classroom instruction and will be expected to maintain strong ties with industry to incorporate the latest pedagogical trends into the classroom to prepare students for jobs post-graduation. The successful candidate(s) will be expected to teach courses at the graduate and undergraduate level. Preferred candidates should be able to teach one or more of the following areas in addition to Strategic Communication: Web Design, Podcasting, Social Media, Sports & Entertainment Production, Public Relations, Documentary Filmmaking, Communication Theory and/or Research. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. in Communication from an accredited university by the hire date. DESIRED KNOWLEDGE, ABILITIES AND SKILLS Must be proficient in sports/entertainment production, social media, content creation and data analytics. Experience in one or more: Web Design, Podcasting, Live Production, Public Relations, Communication Theory and/or Research. The ability to teach in a 100% asynchronous online delivery format, hybrid or face to face. Ability to interact with students and graduate faculty. REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter Resume/Vita Copies of Transcripts (Only an unofficial transcript for the Highest degree is required at application. Official transcripts for all degrees will be required upon employment.) Posting Close Date December 8, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Graphics-Designer_R-2598": {
      "title": "Graphics Designer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University’s Department of University Marketing and Communications invites applications for the position of Graphic Designer. Southeastern Louisiana University is seeking a creative, detail-oriented, and collaborative Graphic Designer to develop compelling visual communications across print and digital platforms. The Graphic Designer will create materials that support the organization's marketing, communications, promotional, and branding initiatives while maintaining a consistent and professional visual identity. The candidate will be comfortable taking projects from concept through final production, managing multiple projects and deadlines, and collaborating with colleagues, vendors, photographers, and other creative professionals. As part of UMC's Creative Team, the graphic designer will also help with occasional planning, scheduling, and physical set-up of photo and video shoots. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree in Graphic Design, Visual Communication, Fine Arts, or a related field by hire date. At least 1 year of professional graphic design experience. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience working in a marketing, communications, advertising, or corporate creative environment. Experience with photography, photo editing. Experience creating social media and digital marketing content. Experience developing or working within established brand guidelines. Experience coordinating projects with printers, sign companies, promotional vendors, or other outside production partners. Knowledge of accessibility considerations for print and digital communications. Experience managing multiple projects from concept through final production. DESIRED KNOWLEDGE, ABILITIES, AND SKILLS Demonstrated proficiency with Adobe Creative Cloud, particularly: Adobe InDesign, Adobe Illustrator, and Adobe Photoshop Strong understanding of typography, layout, composition, color, hierarchy, and visual communication. Experience creating materials for both print and digital platforms. Ability to prepare production-ready files for print and digital distribution. Strong attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Ability to manage multiple projects, priorities, and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively with individuals across different departments and areas of expertise. Demonstrated ability to receive feedback and make revisions effectively. Strong organizational and file-management skills. Must provide a professional portfolio demonstrating relevant design experience. REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter Resume/Vita Copies of Transcripts (official transcripts will be required if hired) Names and contact information for 3 references. An attached portfolio or link to digital portfolio demonstrating graphic design abilities and creative process to include: Print publications Marketing and promotional materials Branding and identity projects Digital graphics Social media graphics Advertising Editorial design Photography or photo editing Presentation design Illustration or other visual communication work Posting Close Date October 22, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Laborer-Horticultural-Attendant_R-2622": {
      "title": "Laborer/Horticultural Attendant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nSoutheastern Louisiana University’s Department of Physical Plant Services invites applications for the position of Laborer/Horticultural Attendant. This position maintains turf and landscapes in an assigned area of campus under the guidance of a Horticulturist supervisor. Turf-maintenance duties include mowing, string trimming, edging, and blowing. Landscape maintenance includes pruning, mulching, weed control, and chemical applications. This position may assist with landscape installation and planting projects. This is a career progression position in which a new incumbent may be hired as a Laborer if they do not meet the minimum qualifications for Horticultural Attendant. For incumbents hired as Laborers, after minimum qualifications for Horticultural Attendant are met and satisfactory performance has been established, the incumbent may then be moved to the Horticultural Attendant job title. Hourly Rate: $10.70/ $16.06 Schedule: Mon - Fri 6:00 am – 2:30 pm, 30-minute lunch MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS One year of experience or training in farming, the care and maintenance of trees and shrubs, or groundskeeping; OR Six semester hours in a plant science or landscape field of study. When applying, you should list all Education and Work Experience on this application. When listing your Work Experience, indicate if the job was full-time or part-time and what percentage of time you spent on each of the duties listed. This information will be used to determine if you meet the Minimum Qualifications of the position. If complete information is not listed, it may result in your application not being considered. *Resumes WILL NOT be accepted in lieu of completed education and experience sections on your application.  Applicants must possess a valid driver’s license and be able to be certified through the Southeastern Defensive Driving Course.   Click Here to View the Civil Service Job Spec Posting Close Date October 26, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. HR Contact If you have questions about this position, the application process or need special accommodations, please call the Human Resources Office at (985) 549-2001 or send an email to jobs@southeastern.edu."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Assistant-Professor-of-Communication-and-Media-Studies_R-2611": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Communication and Media Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. The Department of Communication and Media Studies at Southeastern Louisiana University invites applications for one (1) tenure-track Assistant Professor position. We seek dynamic teacher-scholars with expertise in Strategic Communication and digital media, with a strong understanding of how these tools function in commercial contexts. Candidates should be well-versed in social media, content marketing, and data analytics, and prepared to train students to become strategic communicators and content creators for industry. As part of an applied program focused on career readiness, the successful candidates will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in online, asynchronous instruction, and maintain active engagement with industry partners to bring current trends and best practices into the classroom. Faculty will teach at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. In addition to Strategic Communication, preference will be given to candidates with the ability to teach in one or more of the following areas: Video Production, Podcasting, Strategic Communication, Persuasion, Public Relations, Communication Theory, and/or Research. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. in Communication from an accredited university by hire date Demonstrated proficiency in social media, digital advertising, content marketing, and data analytics DESIRED KNOWLEDGE, ABILITIES AND SKILLS Experience teaching in a variety of delivery formats, including 100% asynchronous online, hybrid, and face-to-face modalities Ability to effectively engage with both undergraduate and graduate students Experience teaching in one or more of the following areas: Video Production, Podcasting, Strategic Communication, Persuasion, Public Relations, Communication Theory, and/or Research. REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter Resume/Vita Copies of Transcripts (Only an unofficial transcript for the Highest degree is required at application. Official transcripts for all degrees will be required upon employment.) Posting Close Date November 10, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Administrative-Assistant-3_R-2615": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant 3",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nSoutheastern Louisiana University’s Office of Financial Aid invites applications for the position of Administrative Assistant 3. The Administrative Assistant 3 provides comprehensive, high-level administrative, clerical, and operational support to both the Director of Financial Aid and the broader Financial Aid Office. This position serves as a central hub for office operations, ensuring seamless daily workflows, supervising student personnel, and delivering exceptional customer service to students, parents, and university staff. Hourly Rate: $13.77 AN IDEAL CANDIDATE SHOULD POSSESS THE FOLLOWING COMPETENCIES Communicating Effectively : The ability to relay information correctly and appropriately to connect people and ideas Demonstrating Accountability : The ability to accept ownership for your actions, behaviors, performance, and decisions Focusing on Customers:  The ability to serve the needs of those who support and/or rely on the services provided EXAMS AND LICENSE REQUIRMENTS No Civil Service test score is required in order to be considered for this vacancy Applicants must possess a valid driver’s license and be able to be certified through the Southeastern Defensive Driving Course MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS Two years of experience in administrative services. SUBSTITUTIONS Every 15 semester hours earned from an accredited college or university will be credited as six months of experience. Failure to provide your qualifying work experience will result in your application not being considered Any qualifying experience that is based on college credit/hours will require a transcript for verification Any college hours or degree must be from a school accredited by one of the following regional accrediting bodies:  the Middle States Commission on Higher Education; the New England Association of Schools and Colleges; the Higher Learning Commission; the Northwest Commission on Colleges and Universities; the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools; and the Western Association of Schools and Colleges. When applying, you should list all Education and Work Experience on this application. When listing your Work Experience, indicate if the job was full-time or part-time and what percentage of time you spent on each of the duties listed. This information will be used to determine if you meet the Minimum Qualifications of the position. If complete information is not listed, it may result in your application not being considered. *Resumes WILL NOT be accepted in lieu of completed education and experience sections on your application. There is no guarantee that everyone who applies to this posting will be interviewed. The hiring supervisor/manager has 90 days from the closing date of the posting to make a hiring decision. Click Here to View the Civil Service Job Spec   Posting Close Date October 27, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. HR Contact If you have questions about this position, the application process or need special accommodations, please call the Human Resources Office at (985) 549-2001 or send an email to jobs@southeastern.edu."
