    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Vice-President-for-University-Advancement_R-2629": {
      "title": "Vice President for University Advancement",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University seeks a dynamic, visionary, and experienced leader to serve as Vice President for University Advancement. Reporting directly to the President, the Vice President for University Advancement serves as a key member of the executive leadership team, providing strategic leadership to advance the university’s mission, vision, and goals through philanthropic support, and alumni engagement. This position will oversee a comprehensive advancement program, including development, alumni relations, fostering relationships that enhance the university’s profile, secure resources, and promote Southeastern’s role as a leading institution of higher education. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS - Master's degree required; terminal degree preferred - Senior leadership experience in higher education, economic development, innovation, industry, government, or a related field - Demonstrated success in strategic planning, delivering measurable outcomes through partnerships, and external engagement - Strong strategic planning, financial, negotiation, and strategic execution skills PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS - Experience with regional public universities, economic development, and innovation ecosystems - Track record in public-private partnerships, capital projects, and revenue-generating initiatives - Established relationships with industry, investors, philanthropic partners, and community leaders - Familiarity with the Southeast Louisiana region and its philanthropic community DESIRED KNOWLEDGE, ABILITIES AND SKILLS - Demonstrated success in major gift fundraising, capital campaigns, and donor relations - Proven ability to lead and manage a diverse team and foster a culture of accountability and excellence - Exceptional interpersonal and communication skills - Strategic thinker with a results-oriented approach - Ability to build and maintain strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders - Strong commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in all aspects of advancement work REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter Resume/Vita Copies of Transcripts (official transcripts will be required if hired) Names and Contact Information for 3 References Posting Close Date November 11, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/eResources-and-Web-Services-Librarian--Instructor-_R-2620": {
      "title": "eResources and Web Services Librarian (Instructor)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University's Sims Memorial Library invites applications for the position of eResources and Web Services Librarian. Reporting to the Head of Electronic Resources and Serials, this position is charged with primary responsibility for the implementation and management of electronic resources (including online journals and databases) as well as oversight of the Library’s Web presence (including creating and maintaining the Library’s Web pages). This position also serves as the Assistant Electronic Resources and Serials Librarian and works as a member of the departmental team in providing efficient and effective service to students, faculty, staff, and the local community. Additionally, this position assists the Outreach Librarian with social media and digital signage as needed. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree (ALA-accredited MLS or MLIS) PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS 3 to 5 years of work-related experience Microsoft Office/Google Suite (Word/Docs, Powerpoint/Slides, Excel/Sheets, Outlook/Gmail) Database and proxy server administration (library-related) Web Development Statistical software (library-related) ILS/LMS software (library-related) REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter Resume/Vita Copies of Transcripts (Only an unofficial transcript for the Highest degree is required at application. Official transcripts for all degrees will be required upon employment.) Posting Close Date November 16, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    }
